Fri Oct 23 06:54:06 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.10.0 (upstream tag v0.10.0, 2026-10-22):
  * Linux window frame is now decided by the shared craft-window
    crate: KDE, Sway, Hyprland, COSMIC and X11 keep the native
    titlebar, GNOME keeps the app-drawn one; FIGCRAFT_TITLEBAR=app
    or system overrides it.
  * Components: Combine as variants in the context menu and Design
    panel, Add variant on a lone component, new component sets named
    from the variant path.
  * Saved documents show their chosen filename, comment drafts are
    dismissed on tool switch, a document dropped on the canvas opens
    as a new file, the pages list keeps the current page in view.
  * Fixes: CSS colour parsing rejects malformed alpha and extra
    arguments, same-server check strips the default port when the
    address has a path, whole numbers beyond the i64 range print
    correctly, SVG export Title Case no longer restarts mid-word
    across styled runs, reversed open subpaths stay open, local
    links reject non-hex tokens.
  * UTC/calendar conversion uses chrono instead of hand-rolled code;
    packaging scripts enforce HTTPS on curl downloads.
  * Re-vendored with update=false against the upstream lockfile:
    adds craft-window (second craft-libs git rev) and chrono, plus
    patch bumps (rustls, rustls-webpki, webpki-roots, zip, uuid).
    Every new or changed crate in the shipped targets is under
    licences already listed (MIT, Apache-2.0, ISC, BSD-2-Clause,
    CDLA-Permissive-2.0, Unicode-3.0), so License is unchanged; no
    copyleft added, no new system deps, MSRV still 1.95.
  * Vendor audit: no RUSTSEC advisories reported.
- Set the fixed metainfo release date to 2026-10-22 (v0.10.0); it
  still carried the v0.6.0 date.

